From 9bfc3ef2c99d93677a950bfdfc0eced94f8c1ce9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <hades@libreelec.tv>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:24:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: integrate Dolby Vision STB 2.6 native engine

Integrate the official Dolby Vision STB 2.6 industrial-grade core
algorithms into the dvbridge pipeline, guarded by both the GUI setting
videoscreen.hadesdvstb26 (Settings > System > Display) and the global
switch <dovistb26engine> in advancedsettings.xml (default: true).

The STB 2.6 engine provides complete algorithmic capabilities:
1. Complete RPU and Extension Blocks (L1-L11, L254, L255) with CPU-side
   bit-level fast MEL detection and safe Active Area (L5) geometry
   consolidation that falls back to full raster without assertions.
2. Official Display Management 2.6 with target VSVDB V0/V1/V2 modeling,
   3-segment S-curve tone mapping and 2-pass Trim interpolation
   generating a 4096-step LUT saturated at 4095.
3. Fixed-point color matrix engine supporting RGB, YUV, LMS, IPT, and
   ICtCp color spaces with cross-talk elimination.
4. HDMI wire and transport defense with dynamic trim reduction to keep
   metadata within hardware capacity (509/482 bytes) and temporal IIR
   filtering to eliminate backlight breathing.
